    {
      "id": "nvda-mdna-datacenter",
      "type": "narrative",
      "answer": "In NVIDIA's fiscal 2026 10-K MD&A, Data Center revenue rose 68% year over year. NVIDIA attributes the growth to the major platform shifts to accelerated computing and AI. Data Center computing grew 59% on demand for the Blackwell platform, which made up most of Data Center revenue. Data Center networking grew 142%, driven by the introduction and ramp of NVLink compute fabric for GB200 and GB300 systems and by growth in Ethernet and InfiniBand.",
